<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wallia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 415–418</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wallia was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from 415 to 418. After a failed attempt to cross to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, he made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, returned the captive Galla Placidia and fought for the empire in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>, destroying the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siling-vandals">Siling Vandals</a> and crushing the Alans. In 418 Rome rewarded the Visigoths with settlement as federates in Aquitaine, where his successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-i">Theodoric I</a> founded the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wallia.jpg" alt="Wallia" width="320" height="521" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alejo Vera · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Walia,_rey_de_los_Visigodos_(Museo_del_Prado).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
